{"course": {"id": "s15", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Primary Mathematics — Stage 5", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "The Number System"}, {"n": 2, "t": "2D Shapes"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Numbers and Sequences"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Averages"}, {"n": 5, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (1)"}, {"n": 6, "t": "3D Shapes"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Fractions, Decimals and Percentages"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (2)"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Angles"}, {"n": 11, "t": "Multiplication and Division"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Data"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Ratio and Proportion"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Area and Perimeter"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Multiplying and Dividing Fractions and Decimals"}, {"n": 16, "t": "Time"}, {"n": 17, "t": "Number and the Laws of Arithmetic"}, {"n": 18, "t": "Position and Direction"}]}, "unit": {"n": 4, "stage": 15, "title": "Averages", "strandShort": "Statistics and probability", "blurb": "Finding the mode and the median of a set of data, and using them to describe and compare data.", "strand": "Statistics and probability", "framework": "Cambridge Primary Mathematics (0096), Stage 5", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m5u04.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"code": "5Ss.03", "sec": "4.1", "codeNote": "", "t": "Find and interpret the mode of a set of data, including data with no mode or more than one mode."}, "O2": {"code": "5Ss.04", "sec": "4.2", "codeNote": "", "t": "Find and interpret the median of a set of data."}}, "sections": [{"id": "4.1", "title": "The mode", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "idea", "t": "What is the mode?", "p": ["The **mode** is the value that appears **most often**. It is the most **popular** answer.", "In the bar chart, banana has the tallest bar, so **banana** is the mode of the favourite fruits."], "fig": {"kind": "barchart", "labels": ["apple", "banana", "mango", "orange"], "values": [4, 9, 6, 3], "ymax": 10, "step": 2, "ylabel": "Children"}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Can there be no mode or two modes?", "p": ["If every value appears the **same number of times**, there is **no mode**: 2, 4, 6, 8.", "If two values are equally most common, there are **two modes**: 3, 3, 5, 7, 7 → modes 3 and 7."]}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I find the mode?", "p": ["Step 1: Put the data in order or make a tally.", "Step 2: Count how many times each value appears.", "Step 3: The value with the biggest count is the mode."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Numbers", "p": [], "q": "Find the mode of 6, 2, 9, 6, 4, 2, 6.", "steps": [["6 appears 3 times; 2 appears twice", ""]], "a": "6"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Words", "p": [], "q": "Pets: cat, dog, fish, dog, cat, dog. What is the mode?", "steps": [["dog 3, cat 2, fish 1", ""]], "a": "dog"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "The mode is the frequency?", "p": ["The mode is the **value** (dog), not how many times it appears (3)."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Tally first", "p": ["A tally chart makes counting each value quick and stops you missing any."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 300, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "4.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": -1, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u04s1k02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Before you read on: what is the mode of 3, 5, 5, 7, 8?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "options": [{"t": "7", "ok": false, "fb": "The mode is the most common value."}, {"t": "5", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}, {"t": "5.6", "ok": false, "fb": "That is the mean."}]}}, {"id": "4.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u04s1k01", "type": "short", "prompt": "Favourite fruits: apple, mango, apple, pear, mango, apple. What is the mode?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["apple", "Apple"]}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 300]], "req": [{"id": "m5u04s1r01", "type": "short", "prompt": "The bar chart shows favourite fruits. What is the mode?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "accept": ["mango", "Mango"], "fig": {"kind": "barchart", "labels": ["apple", "banana", "mango", "orange"], "values": [3, 4, 8, 6], "ymax": 10, "step": 2, "ylabel": "Children"}}, {"id": "m5u04s1r02", "type": "num", "prompt": "The table shows shoe sizes in a group. What is the modal shoe size?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "answer": 30, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "data": {"head": ["Size", "22", "24", "26", "28", "30"], "rows": [["Children", "2", "3", "1", "4", "5"]]}, "bare": true}, {"id": "m5u04s1r03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Find the mode of 5, 2, 3, 16, 5, 5.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m5u04s1r04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "What is the mode of 11, 26, 4, 24, 1?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "options": [{"t": "there is no mode", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}, {"t": "1", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "26", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "11", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}]}, {"id": "m5u04s1r05", "type": "table", "prompt": "Dice scores: 1, 2, 6, 6, 1, 3, 2, 5, 2, 5. Complete the tally table.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "head": ["Score", "1", "2", "3", "4", "5", "6"], "rows": [["Frequency", {"ans": 2}, {"ans": 3}, {"ans": 1}, {"ans": 0}, {"ans": 2}, {"ans": 2}]]}, {"id": "m5u04s1r06", "type": "short", "prompt": "The table shows how many goals were scored in some matches. What is the modal number of goals?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "accept": ["4"], "data": {"head": ["Goals", "0", "1", "2", "3", "4"], "rows": [["Matches", "6", "7", "2", "4", "8"]]}}, {"id": "m5u04s1r07", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "What are the modes of 16, 2, 1, 2, 1?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "options": [{"t": "there is no mode", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "16", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "1 and 2", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}, {"t": "1 only", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}]}, {"id": "m5u04s1r08", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain why 2, 3, 4, 5 has no mode.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "each value appears only once", "kw": ["once|same number|each"]}, {"pt": "no value appears more often than the others", "kw": ["no value|none|more often"]}], "model": "Every value appears exactly once, so no value appears more often than the others. There is no mode.", "need": 1, "reason": "Every value appears exactly once, so no value appears more often than the others. There is no mode."}], "prac": [{"id": "m5u04s1p01", "type": "short", "prompt": "The bar chart shows favourite fruits. What is the mode?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "accept": ["orange", "Orange"], "fig": {"kind": "barchart", "labels": ["apple", "banana", "mango", "orange"], "values": [3, 6, 4, 7], "ymax": 10, "step": 2, "ylabel": "Children"}}, {"id": "m5u04s1p02", "type": "num", "prompt": "The table shows shoe sizes in a group. What is the modal shoe size?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "answer": 26, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "data": {"head": ["Size", "22", "24", "26", "28", "30"], "rows": [["Children", "1", "3", "5", "2", "4"]]}, "bare": true}, {"id": "m5u04s1p03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Find the mode of 3, 3, 11, 8, 3, 2.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m5u04s1p04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "What is the mode of 27, 13, 22, 7, 29?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "options": [{"t": "7", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "there is no mode", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}, {"t": "29", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "27", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}]}, {"id": "m5u04s1p05", "type": "table", "prompt": "Dice scores: 4, 1, 6, 1, 5, 4, 6, 2, 2, 2. Complete the tally table.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "head": ["Score", "1", "2", "3", "4", "5", "6"], "rows": [["Frequency", {"ans": 2}, {"ans": 3}, {"ans": 0}, {"ans": 2}, {"ans": 1}, {"ans": 2}]]}, {"id": "m5u04s1p06", "type": "short", "prompt": "The table shows how many goals were scored in some matches. What is the modal number of goals?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "accept": ["2"], "data": {"head": ["Goals", "0", "1", "2", "3", "4"], "rows": [["Matches", "2", "6", "8", "3", "7"]]}}, {"id": "m5u04s1p07", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "What are the modes of 13, 13, 10, 16, 10?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "options": [{"t": "10 only", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "there is no mode", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "10 and 13", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}, {"t": "16", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}]}, {"id": "m5u04s1p08", "type": "num", "prompt": "The numbers 4, 4, 8, 10, 9 have mode 4. Which number could you add so that 4 is still the only mode?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}], "adv": [{"id": "m5u04s1a01", "type": "short", "prompt": "* Advanced. The bar chart shows favourite fruits. What is the mode?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "accept": ["banana", "Banana"], "fig": {"kind": "barchart", "labels": ["apple", "banana", "mango", "orange"], "values": [2, 7, 3, 6], "ymax": 10, "step": 2, "ylabel": "Children"}}, {"id": "m5u04s1a02", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. Find the mode of 19, 9, 6, 19, 19, 17.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 19, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m5u0